3:["$","div",null,{"lang":"en","children":[["$","$Le",null,{"lang":"en","items":[{"id":"001","slug":"distribution-is-the-moat","category":"doctrine","term":"Account-Generated Distribution","en":{"title":"Content is cheap. Distribution isn’t.","dek":"Everyone can produce. Almost nobody knows how to distribute. Welcome to the other side of the iceberg."}},{"id":"002","slug":"ai-sameness","category":"creative","term":"AI Slop","en":{"title":"AI isn’t the problem. Sameness is.","dek":"Perfect faces. Interchangeable scripts. Creativity is not measured in exports per minute."}},{"id":"003","slug":"account-isolation","category":"doctrine","term":"Account Isolation","en":{"title":"50 accounts. One idea. Zero strategy.","dek":"Account Isolation: differentiate the voices before multiplying the profiles."}},{"id":"004","slug":"native-vs-api","category":"lab","term":"Native Posting","en":{"title":"Does native really win? Show the data.","dek":"“APIs kill reach.” Here is the protocol that claim would need."}},{"id":"005","slug":"agent-first-dry-run","category":"machines","term":"Agentic AGD","en":{"title":"Your agent can publish. Teach it to wait.","dek":"A real MCP workflow starts with a readable preview, not a surprise charge."}},{"id":"006","slug":"multi-account-strategy","category":"doctrine","term":"Multi-Account Strategy","en":{"title":"One brand account cannot carry everything.","dek":"A Multi-Account Strategy distributes a brand’s experiments across differentiated accounts."}},{"id":"007","slug":"content-isolation","category":"doctrine","term":"Content Isolation","en":{"title":"New subtitles do not make a new idea.","dek":"Content Isolation preserves meaningful creative differences between accounts: narrative, angle, format or purpose."}},{"id":"008","slug":"content-saturation","category":"doctrine","term":"Content Saturation","en":{"title":"The feed did not add hours to the day.","dek":"Content Saturation describes content supply exceeding available attention."}},{"id":"009","slug":"feed-escalation","category":"doctrine","term":"Feed Escalation","en":{"title":"Welcome to the feed arms race.","dek":"Feed Escalation is our editorial term for intensifying formats, output and optimization inside feeds."}},{"id":"010","slug":"attention-war","category":"doctrine","term":"Attention War","en":{"title":"Your SaaS competes with cat videos too.","dek":"Attention War is our cultural shorthand for competition over limited attention among content, people and platforms."}},{"id":"011","slug":"agd-not-phone-farm","category":"doctrine","term":"Phone Farming","en":{"title":"A row of phones is not a strategy.","dek":"Phone Farming describes infrastructure for operating accounts across mobile environments."}},{"id":"012","slug":"agd-without-tokportal","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD & infrastructure","en":{"title":"AGD must outlive the name of its vendor.","dek":"AGD is a strategy framework. TokPortal provides infrastructure that can support execution. A category that only works with one brand mostly looks like a campaign."}},{"id":"013","slug":"ten-principles","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD principles","en":{"title":"A small manifesto for accounts with a reason to exist.","dek":"AGD principles combine differentiated accounts, creative diversity, contextual execution and measurable learning."}},{"id":"014","slug":"anti-principles","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD anti-principles","en":{"title":"What we refuse to sell as growth.","dek":"AGD anti-principles challenge clones, volume without diversity, certainty without data and averages without context."}},{"id":"015","slug":"native-account","category":"doctrine","term":"Native Account","en":{"title":"Native is an environment, not a talisman.","dek":"In the AGD lexicon, a Native Account is created and maintained in the real consumer application environment."}},{"id":"016","slug":"account-persona","category":"creative","term":"Account Persona","en":{"title":"A persona is not a photo and a name.","dek":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return.."}},{"id":"017","slug":"hook-slop","category":"creative","term":"Hook Slop","en":{"title":"“Stop scrolling”: everybody is shouting the same thing.","dek":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value."}},{"id":"018","slug":"faceless-account","category":"creative","term":"Faceless Account","en":{"title":"Faceless. Not voiceless.","dek":"A Faceless Account creates content without relying on its operator’s visible face."}},{"id":"019","slug":"formatted-account","category":"creative","term":"Formatted Account","en":{"title":"A recurring format beats an empty template.","dek":"A Formatted Account uses a repeatable creative structure an audience can recognize."}},{"id":"020","slug":"chaotic-account","category":"creative","term":"Chaotic Account","en":{"title":"A chaotic account still has a point of view.","dek":"A Chaotic Account allows several formats rather than one rigid template."}},{"id":"021","slug":"ai-persona","category":"creative","term":"AI Persona","en":{"title":"A synthetic character needs something to say.","dek":"An AI Persona substantially uses AI for appearance, voice or production."}},{"id":"022","slug":"persona-agd","category":"creative","term":"Persona AGD","en":{"title":"One product. Three narrators. Three reasons.","dek":"Persona AGD organizes a network around distinct editorial characters rather than generic brand accounts.."}},{"id":"023","slug":"slideshow-agd","category":"creative","term":"Slideshow AGD","en":{"title":"A slideshow is a story, not a sliced PDF.","dek":"Slideshow AGD uses accounts publishing native carousels or slideshows."}},{"id":"024","slug":"story-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Story Slideshow","en":{"title":"A little tension beats fifteen advice slides.","dek":"A Story Slideshow organizes a sequence around a situation and its resolution."}},{"id":"025","slug":"educational-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Educational Slideshow","en":{"title":"Teach something before the final slide.","dek":"An educational slideshow communicates usable knowledge during reading."}},{"id":"026","slug":"meme-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Meme Slideshow","en":{"title":"The joke should work without the logo.","dek":"A Meme Slideshow builds its sequence around a cultural observation or punchline."}},{"id":"027","slug":"product-discovery","category":"creative","term":"Product Discovery","en":{"title":"The product enters when it becomes useful.","dek":"Product discovery content introduces a tool inside an understandable use case."}},{"id":"028","slug":"brainrotization","category":"creative","term":"Brainrotization","en":{"title":"Marketing caught brainrot. What next?","dek":"Brainrotization is our cultural shorthand for fast, absurd and compressed feed formats."}},{"id":"029","slug":"creative-brief","category":"creative","term":"Creative Brief","en":{"title":"A good brief starts with what we want to learn.","dek":"An AGD creative brief connects audience, promise, format and hypothesis."}},{"id":"030","slug":"hook-payoff","category":"creative","term":"Hook & payoff","en":{"title":"The hook’s promise must be paid back.","dek":"The payoff is the narrative or practical answer to the opening promise."}},{"id":"031","slug":"creative-library","category":"creative","term":"Creative Library","en":{"title":"Your creative library is not a final_final folder.","dek":"A creative library organizes concepts, versions, rights and results."}},{"id":"032","slug":"format-fatigue","category":"creative","term":"Format fatigue","en":{"title":"The format works. Until it just repeats.","dek":"Format fatigue is a hypothesis about weakening response after repetition."}},{"id":"033","slug":"creative-matrix","category":"creative","term":"Creative Matrix","en":{"title":"The matrix that stops fifty copies from being born.","dek":"A creative matrix crosses variation dimensions: audience, problem, angle and format."}},{"id":"034","slug":"niche-warming","category":"field-notes","term":"Niche Warming","en":{"title":"Warm an account without invoking magic.","dek":"Niche Warming means exploring niche content in the app through searches, viewing and authentic interactions."}},{"id":"035","slug":"native-posting","category":"field-notes","term":"Native Posting","en":{"title":"Native posting: the action matters, so does the brief.","dek":"Native Posting means publishing through a platform’s consumer interface."}},{"id":"036","slug":"native-warming","category":"field-notes","term":"Native Warming","en":{"title":"Warming is not a robot dance.","dek":"Native Warming happens in the real application through ordinary, authentic interactions."}},{"id":"037","slug":"geo-targeted-account","category":"field-notes","term":"Geo-Targeted Account","en":{"title":"A US account does not guarantee a US audience.","dek":"A Geo-Targeted Account is established and operated in its target market."}},{"id":"038","slug":"geo-posting","category":"field-notes","term":"Geo-Posting","en":{"title":"Localization starts before the publish button.","dek":"Geo-Posting means publishing through an account operated in the target market."}},{"id":"039","slug":"us-launch","category":"field-notes","term":"US launch","en":{"title":"Launching in the US from abroad: start with the scene.","dek":"An international launch needs an understandable offer and a locally relevant use case."}},{"id":"040","slug":"localization-not-translation","category":"field-notes","term":"Localization","en":{"title":"Translate the words. Then rebuild the situation.","dek":"Localization adapts meaning, references and uses."}},{"id":"041","slug":"account-brief","category":"field-notes","term":"Account Brief","en":{"title":"The account brief fits on one page.","dek":"An account brief sets its promise, audience, voice and boundaries."}},{"id":"042","slug":"operator-handoff","category":"field-notes","term":"Operator handoff","en":{"title":"The handoff that prevents “I thought you meant”.","dek":"A handoff transfers an executable task with assets, constraints and success conditions."}},{"id":"043","slug":"publishing-window","category":"field-notes","term":"Publishing window","en":{"title":"A publishing window beats a sacred minute.","dek":"A publishing window defines an acceptable interval for a task."}},{"id":"044","slug":"account-inventory","category":"field-notes","term":"Account inventory","en":{"title":"Your network starts with an accurate inventory.","dek":"An AGD inventory connects each account to its role, market, owner and observed state."}},{"id":"045","slug":"zero-views","category":"field-notes","term":"Stuck at 0 views","en":{"title":"Zero views is not a diagnosis.","dek":"Stuck at 0 views describes low or absent distribution after publication."}},{"id":"046","slug":"shadowban","category":"field-notes","term":"Shadowban","en":{"title":"Shadowban is sometimes the name we give the unknown.","dek":"Shadowban is an informal term for suspected distribution suppression without explicit notice."}},{"id":"047","slug":"distribution-failure","category":"field-notes","term":"Distribution failure","en":{"title":"Different failures hidden inside “it does not work”.","dek":"A distribution failure can involve account access, a feature, removed content, a missing publication or weak reach."}},{"id":"048","slug":"native-not-deceptive","category":"field-notes","term":"Commercial transparency","en":{"title":"Organic does not mean undercover.","dek":"Content can be useful, native and commercial at once."}},{"id":"049","slug":"reddit-agd","category":"field-notes","term":"Reddit AGD","en":{"title":"On Reddit, context is the entrance.","dek":"Reddit AGD adapts account differentiation to legitimate community participation."}},{"id":"050","slug":"community-distribution","category":"field-notes","term":"Community distribution","en":{"title":"Participate before distributing.","dek":"A community is not merely an acquisition channel."}},{"id":"051","slug":"content-rights","category":"field-notes","term":"Content rights","en":{"title":"An asset folder needs evidence, not assumptions.","dek":"A provenance register connects images, sounds and videos to their origins and checked usage conditions."}},{"id":"052","slug":"campaign-retrospective","category":"field-notes","term":"Campaign retrospective","en":{"title":"A retrospective starts with what we do not know.","dek":"An AGD retrospective connects objectives, execution, observations and decisions."}},{"id":"053","slug":"budget-of-learning","category":"field-notes","term":"Learning budget","en":{"title":"A test also costs the time spent making sense of it.","dek":"A learning budget includes production, coordination, execution and analysis."}},{"id":"054","slug":"viral-hit","category":"lab","term":"Viral Hit","en":{"title":"Viral compared with what?","dek":"A Viral Hit is an unusually high distribution outcome relative to a defined baseline: account, cohort or campaign."}},{"id":"055","slug":"viral-hit-rate","category":"lab","term":"Viral Hit Rate","en":{"title":"The denominator is half the story.","dek":"Viral Hit Rate is the proportion of eligible posts exceeding a predefined outlier threshold."}},{"id":"056","slug":"median-vs-mean","category":"lab","term":"Median vs mean","en":{"title":"The average loves an overly good story.","dek":"The mean adds values and divides by their count."}},{"id":"057","slug":"percentiles","category":"lab","term":"Distribution percentiles","en":{"title":"P90 is not a new word for good.","dek":"A percentile locates a value in an ordered distribution."}},{"id":"058","slug":"power-law","category":"lab","term":"Distribution concentration","en":{"title":"The hit makes noise. The rest explains the system.","dek":"Concentration measures the share of outcomes produced by a fraction of posts."}},{"id":"059","slug":"top-ten-accounts","category":"lab","term":"Account concentration","en":{"title":"The network works. Or one account carries it.","dek":"Account concentration shows which assets carry the total outcome."}},{"id":"060","slug":"matched-cohorts","category":"lab","term":"Matched cohorts","en":{"title":"Compare what is actually comparable.","dek":"A matched cohort aligns observations on known characteristics."}},{"id":"061","slug":"posting-time-myth","category":"lab","term":"Posting-time myth","en":{"title":"7:42 p.m. is not a strategy.","dek":"Posting-time effects may depend on audience and context."}},{"id":"062","slug":"posting-frequency","category":"lab","term":"Posting frequency","en":{"title":"Posting more: more chances or more noise?","dek":"A frequency test must separate total volume, per-post performance and production load."}},{"id":"063","slug":"warming-study","category":"lab","term":"Warming protocol","en":{"title":"Warming deserves more than an anecdote.","dek":"A warming protocol compares preparations defined before publishing."}},{"id":"064","slug":"account-age","category":"lab","term":"Account age","en":{"title":"An old account is not a control group.","dek":"Account age can be associated with history, followers and behavior."}},{"id":"065","slug":"slideshow-vs-video","category":"lab","term":"Slideshow vs video","en":{"title":"Slideshow versus video: context comes first.","dek":"Comparing slideshow and video requires a comparable promise and audience."}},{"id":"066","slug":"formatted-vs-chaotic","category":"lab","term":"Formatted vs chaotic","en":{"title":"Series or chaos? A test, not a taste war.","dek":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats."}},{"id":"067","slug":"creative-diversity-test","category":"lab","term":"Creative diversity","en":{"title":"Diversity also lives in what you learn.","dek":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files."}},{"id":"068","slug":"native-features-test","category":"lab","term":"Native features","en":{"title":"Maybe it is not native. Maybe it is the feature.","dek":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel."}},{"id":"069","slug":"zero-view-rate","category":"lab","term":"Zero-view rate","en":{"title":"A zero rate deserves a complete definition.","dek":"Zero-view rate depends on observation age, measurement source and eligibility scope."}},{"id":"070","slug":"confidence-intervals","category":"lab","term":"Uncertainty","en":{"title":"Uncertainty is part of the result.","dek":"An interval expresses uncertainty under a method’s assumptions."}},{"id":"071","slug":"survivorship-bias","category":"lab","term":"Survivorship bias","en":{"title":"The missing accounts had results too.","dek":"Survivorship bias appears when analysis retains only still-visible units."}},{"id":"072","slug":"regression-to-mean","category":"lab","term":"Regression to the mean","en":{"title":"After a hit, returning to earth is not always a failure.","dek":"An extreme outcome can be followed by more ordinary outcomes."}},{"id":"073","slug":"cohort-maturity","category":"lab","term":"Cohort maturity","en":{"title":"Day seven does not exist for yesterday’s visitor.","dek":"Day-seven conversion should cover people given seven full days to convert."}},{"id":"074","slug":"attribution","category":"lab","term":"Attribution","en":{"title":"A UTM tells you about the click. Not the whole story.","dek":"Campaign parameters describe an instrumented origin."}},{"id":"075","slug":"views-to-buyers","category":"lab","term":"Views to buyers","en":{"title":"A million views can miss the problem.","dek":"Views measure exposure under the platform’s definition."}},{"id":"076","slug":"experiment-preregistration","category":"lab","term":"Preregistration","en":{"title":"Write possible verdicts before knowing the score.","dek":"Preregistering means recording an experiment’s question, criteria and planned analysis in advance."}},{"id":"077","slug":"stop-rules","category":"lab","term":"Stop rules","en":{"title":"Knowing when to stop is part of the test.","dek":"A stop rule specifies when to end, pause or reconsider an experiment."}},{"id":"078","slug":"evidence-ladder","category":"lab","term":"Evidence ladder","en":{"title":"A hypothesis needs a label, not a disguise.","dek":"The AGD evidence ladder separates platform documentation, methodical proprietary data, controlled experiments, repeated observations, hypotheses and folklore."}},{"id":"079","slug":"ai-agd","category":"machines","term":"AI AGD","en":{"title":"AI can think about the system before filling the calendar.","dek":"AI AGD means using AI to plan, produce, analyze or orchestrate AGD."}},{"id":"080","slug":"agentic-agd","category":"machines","term":"Agentic AGD","en":{"title":"A distribution agent is not a talking calendar.","dek":"Agentic AGD coordinates recurring decisions across accounts, content, markets and experiments."}},{"id":"081","slug":"human-api","category":"machines","term":"Human API","en":{"title":"Behind the API, someone actually opens the app.","dek":"A Human API exposes a software workflow partly executed by people."}},{"id":"082","slug":"mcp-orchestration","category":"machines","term":"MCP orchestration","en":{"title":"MCP connects tools. It does not write your strategy.","dek":"MCP lets an agent client discover and call tools exposed by a server."}},{"id":"083","slug":"dry-run-contract","category":"machines","term":"Dry-run contract","en":{"title":"A preview must know what it does not simulate.","dek":"A dry run validates a request without producing live effects under the service’s contract."}},{"id":"084","slug":"idempotency","category":"machines","term":"Idempotency","en":{"title":"Retry without ordering twice.","dek":"Idempotency prevents repeated execution of one intent from producing multiple effects when supported by the operation’s contract."}},{"id":"085","slug":"webhooks","category":"machines","term":"Webhooks","en":{"title":"A webhook reports an event. It does not replace your state.","dek":"A webhook sends an event to your integration."}},{"id":"086","slug":"agent-budget","category":"machines","term":"Agent budgets","en":{"title":"An agent without a ceiling has no budget.","dek":"An agent budget defines authorized operations, limits and renewal conditions."}},{"id":"087","slug":"agent-maturity","category":"machines","term":"AGD maturity model","en":{"title":"Autonomy is a ladder, not a switch.","dek":"The AGD model distinguishes manual work, AI assistance, approved orchestration, agentic management and broader autonomy."}},{"id":"088","slug":"api-slop","category":"machines","term":"API Slop","en":{"title":"Your API is not a distribution strategy.","dek":"API Slop criticizes mass delivery of undifferentiated content without attention to accounts or context."}},{"id":"089","slug":"content-routing","category":"machines","term":"Content routing","en":{"title":"Good content can land on the wrong account.","dek":"Routing connects creative work to an account by audience, persona, market and purpose."}},{"id":"090","slug":"creative-clustering","category":"machines","term":"Creative clustering","en":{"title":"Group ideas without erasing their differences.","dek":"Creative clustering groups content under chosen criteria."}},{"id":"091","slug":"anomaly-detection","category":"machines","term":"Anomaly detection","en":{"title":"A useful alert tells you what to inspect.","dek":"Anomaly detection flags deviation from a defined baseline."}},{"id":"092","slug":"human-review","category":"machines","term":"Human review","en":{"title":"Human review should contain a real decision.","dek":"Useful human review exposes the action, consequences and evidence to check."}},{"id":"093","slug":"source-of-truth","category":"machines","term":"Source of truth","en":{"title":"Documentation that says no beats a page promising everything.","dek":"A technical source of truth describes an interface’s current capabilities."}},{"id":"094","slug":"seo-agd","category":"machines","term":"SEO AGD","en":{"title":"A video can have a second life in search.","dek":"SEO AGD explores social content and properties appearing in search engines and platform search."}},{"id":"095","slug":"pseo-agd","category":"machines","term":"pSEO AGD","en":{"title":"Programmatic content needs a reason for every page.","dek":"pSEO AGD systematically organizes social content around distinct search intents."}},{"id":"096","slug":"llm-quoting","category":"machines","term":"LLM quoting","en":{"title":"To be cited, first be quotable.","dek":"Citable content clearly states a proposition, scope and provenance."}},{"id":"097","slug":"knowledge-graph","category":"machines","term":"AGD content graph","en":{"title":"A good link continues an idea.","dek":"An editorial graph connects parent concepts, neighbors and applications."}},{"id":"098","slug":"multilingual-seo","category":"machines","term":"Multilingual publishing","en":{"title":"Two languages, two real reading experiences.","dek":"A multilingual publication gives each version a stable URL and connects matching translations."}},{"id":"099","slug":"structured-editorial","category":"machines","term":"Structured editorial","en":{"title":"A strict schema frees the voice. It does not write it.","dek":"An editorial schema requires publishing essentials: identity, translations, media, stories, text, sources and links."}},{"id":"100","slug":"agent-audit-log","category":"machines","term":"Agent audit log","en":{"title":"The log that makes tomorrow understandable.","dek":"An agent log connects intent, tool, result and next decision."}}]}],"$Lf","$L10"]}]
11:T505,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Article","@id":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/read/lab/native-vs-api/#article","headline":"Does native really win? Show the data.","description":"“APIs kill reach.” Here is the protocol that claim would need.","inLanguage":"en","datePublished":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","dateModified":"2026-09-08T17:45:45.218Z","image":["https://naybu256.github.io/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"],"author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"THE ORGANIC CLUB Editorial","url":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/about/"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"THE ORGANIC CLUB","url":"https://naybu256.github.io"},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/read/lab/native-vs-api/","articleSection":"The Lab","wordCount":595,"citation":["https://developers.tiktok.com/doc/content-posting-api-get-started/","https://developers.tokportal.com/"]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"THE ORGANIC CLUB","item":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"The Lab","item":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/topics/lab/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Does native really win? Show the data.","item":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/read/lab/native-vs-api/"}]}]}1:["$","main",null,{"id":"main","className":"main-shell","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$11"}}],["$","$L12",null,{"article":{"id":"004","slug":"native-vs-api","category":"lab","term":"Native Posting","kind":"protocol","image":"native-vs-api","tier":"canonical","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":["https://developers.tiktok.com/doc/content-posting-api-get-started/","https://developers.tokportal.com/"],"related":["native-posting","niche-warming","matched-cohorts"],"tokportal":"native","en":{"title":"Does native really win? Show the data.","dek":"“APIs kill reach.” Here is the protocol that claim would need.","point":"Comparing Native Posting with API publishing requires comparable cohorts and identical observation windows. This note reports no experimental result: the verdict remains unknown.","body":["Two screenshots do not make an experiment. An established account posts natively, a new account uses an API, and someone attributes the gap to the upload method. Age, followers, topic and editing quality disappear from the story.","The protocol starts before publication: define eligible accounts, formats, countries and observation windows. Allocate treatments within comparable blocks and retain technical failures. An analysis restricted to successful publications would answer a different question.","Available native features can differ from an integration’s capabilities. Separate two tests: with identical content and features, does the publishing channel change results? And in actual use, does access to native tools change the performance of the complete workflow?","TokPortal illustrates the separation between API orchestration and human execution inside consumer apps. That describes an architecture; it does not prove algorithmic superiority. A conclusion would need a verifiable method and observations."],"action":["Preregister cohorts, primary metric and observation window.","Keep failures in the relevant denominator.","Report median, dispersion and uncertainty."],"trap":"Attributing a creative or account-age difference to the publishing channel.","quote":"An operational preference is not a law of the algorithm.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"An operational preference is not a law of the algorithm.","text":"“APIs kill reach.” Here is the protocol that claim would need.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Native Posting","text":"Comparing Native Posting with API publishing requires comparable cohorts and identical observation windows. This note reports no experimental result: the verdict remains unknown.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Attributing a creative or account-age difference to the publishing channel.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Preregister cohorts, primary metric and observation window.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Keep failures in the relevant denominator.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 3","title":"Report median, dispersion and uncertainty.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"Separate the upload route from the creative package.","paragraphs":["Imagine two posts described as a native-versus-API test. One uses a current sound, an in-app effect and a reply to a comment. The other is a silent export uploaded through a generic workflow. A difference in results would not isolate the upload route. The viewer received different content, and the team may also have chosen different accounts or publishing windows. Before running the comparison, write down every feature available in each workflow and decide which differences belong in the question you are asking.","There are legitimate operational reasons to choose native execution: access to a particular creation surface, an operator’s ability to inspect the final preview, or a workflow the platform exposes only in its own app. Those are capability claims, not evidence of an automatic reach bonus. A useful pilot records the final asset, account context, feature set, publication status and observation window. It also accepts an inconclusive result. If the team cannot hold the creative package reasonably comparable, report the comparison as two production workflows rather than a verdict on an invisible algorithmic preference.","Make a capability table for the actual publishing task before choosing a route. Does this post need a particular in-app effect, an authorised commercial sound, a collaboration setting or an interactive element? Can the supported API perform that operation for this account today? Which steps still require an operator, and how will completion be verified? A plain video upload and a feature-rich native post are different packages. Comparing them without listing those differences lets a technical preference masquerade as an explanation of audience response.","A sensible operation can use more than one route. An API may be appropriate for a supported, repeatable task; an authorised native workflow may be appropriate when a necessary feature is not exposed through that interface. The choice should follow the creative requirements, reliability and cost. Keep a dated record of the capability decision because platform interfaces change. TokPortal's infrastructure is relevant to the execution side of that choice, but its availability does not establish that a native route receives an algorithmic bonus. To investigate distribution, design a comparison that separates the route from the creative features and account histories travelling with it."],"diagram":{"kind":"compare","title":"One comparison, three possible explanations","items":[{"label":"Route","detail":"Where and how the publishing action happened.","value":0},{"label":"Features","detail":"What sounds, replies, effects or formats the viewer received.","value":0},{"label":"Context","detail":"Which account, audience and observation window were involved.","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"The original post can help identify the visible creative package. It cannot tell us which upload route produced it. Keep that boundary intact: a recognisable native-looking format is not evidence about undocumented distribution treatment.","caseIds":[]},"examples":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:45:45.218Z","author":"organic-club-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg","width":1280,"height":849,"alt":{"en":"Keys, indicator lights, and a rotary dial on a vintage wooden telephone switchboard."},"credit":"Antti Leppänen","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 6750269c8667b0eeec97772aa4c8ec3aa97acff4.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orion_%26_Oriola_switchboard_Elisa_Telephone_Museum.jpg","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"}},"lang":"en","next":{"id":"005","slug":"agent-first-dry-run","category":"machines","term":"Agentic AGD","kind":"guide","image":"agent-first-dry-run","tier":"canonical","evidence":"documented","sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/","https://developers.tokportal.com/sandbox/"],"related":["human-api","agentic-agd","idempotency"],"tokportal":"sandbox","en":{"title":"Your agent can publish. Teach it to wait.","dek":"A real MCP workflow starts with a readable preview, not a surprise charge.","point":"TokPortal MCP exposes social operations to an agent. A preview uses top-level dry_run: true, with creation parameters inside body; the decision to execute live remains a separate step.","body":["An agent executing everything quickly is not necessarily a good operator. In a paid workflow, its first useful skill is explaining what it will trigger: country, platform, account and immediate or recurring costs.","The remote server is https://app.tokportal.com/api/ext/mcp. The local package documentation requires version 1.15.1 or later for reliable previews: version 1.15.0 advertised an argument it did not forward correctly. That detail matters more than an impressive agent demo.","Read available countries, prices and balance first. To preview a US TikTok account, tokportal_create_bundle accepts dry_run: true and a body containing bundle_type: account_only, platform: tiktok and country: USA. The response should distinguish simulated credits from charged credits.","Preview identifiers are synthetic. Never reuse them in production. After approval, create real resources and continue with their live identifiers. YouTube bundle creation is not supported through this API in the documentation consulted."],"action":["Read countries, prices and balance before previewing.","Check credits_charged: 0 in the simulated response.","Wait for explicit approval before live creation."],"trap":"A dry run validates a contract; it does not reserve real accounts or capacity.","quote":"Autonomy starts with knowing what still needs a green light.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Autonomy starts with knowing what still needs a green light.","text":"A real MCP workflow starts with a readable preview, not a surprise charge.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Agentic AGD","text":"TokPortal MCP exposes social operations to an agent. A preview uses top-level dry_run: true, with creation parameters inside body; the decision to execute live remains a separate step.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A dry run validates a contract; it does not reserve real accounts or capacity.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Read countries, prices and balance before previewing.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Check credits_charged: 0 in the simulated response.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 3","title":"Wait for explicit approval before live creation.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"Make the preview a contract a person can inspect.","paragraphs":["A dry run earns its name when the reviewer can explain what will happen next without reading the agent’s optimistic narration. For a publishing job, that means the intended account, asset version, caption, time window, cost scope and the action that would cross into real execution. A preview that returns a plausible success message but hides these choices has only moved uncertainty into a nicer interface. Give the reviewer a concrete difference between the current state and the proposed state.","For TokPortal, keep the distinction between a simulated response and a live resource explicit. A synthetic identifier returned by a preview is not something to reuse as if it had been created in production. Before executing a reviewed plan, check current tool documentation and required inputs again, especially when the preview was produced earlier or by another agent. Store the approval against the actual plan revision. If the caption, account or price-sensitive scope changes, the old approval should not silently travel with it. Autonomy becomes useful when the boundary is specific enough to audit.","Treat the preview as a small production meeting with a written agenda. The operator should be able to identify the account or bundle being requested, the country, the quantity, the expected cost and the fact that the operation is still simulated. If the response contains simulated identifiers, keep them out of later live calls. Store the preview beside the proposed inputs, then make any change visible before execution. A dry-run result that nobody reads is only an extra request in the log.","The example payload below is intentionally narrow. It demonstrates the shape of a documented preview request, not a complete autonomous acquisition system. A real workflow must still check current tool capabilities, authorisation, cost and the final live result. If the service returns an uncertain state, reconcile it before retrying. Keep an explicit distinction between prepared, approved, executed and verified. Those states make it possible to give an assistant useful autonomy without treating every fluent completion message as proof that the underlying operation succeeded. The objective is a concrete action a person can understand before it has consequences."],"diagram":{"kind":"flow","title":"A reviewable execution boundary","items":[{"label":"Propose","detail":"Show the exact account, asset and intended action.","value":0},{"label":"Inspect","detail":"Review scope, current capabilities and costs.","value":0},{"label":"Execute","detail":"Use live inputs only after the specific plan is accepted.","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"Treat this public post as the final object a publishing workflow would have to reproduce accurately. The video does not expose the system behind it. The useful exercise is to specify the checks your own agent would need before publishing a comparable asset.","caseIds":[]},"examples":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:45:45.218Z","author":"organic-club-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg","width":1280,"height":976,"alt":{"en":"A red railway signal glows against a deep blue evening sky."},"credit":"W.carter","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 6efd9fae6123d3472d48491b2d5ae91c124f5c48.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_railway_signal_at_dusk.jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"previous":{"id":"003","slug":"account-isolation","category":"doctrine","term":"Account Isolation","kind":"guide","image":"account-isolation","tier":"canonical","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["content-isolation","multi-account-strategy","account-persona"],"en":{"title":"50 accounts. One idea. Zero strategy.","dek":"Account Isolation: differentiate the voices before multiplying the profiles.","point":"Account Isolation is the AGD principle that gives every account a sufficiently distinct identity, audience and purpose to operate as an independent editorial surface.","body":["A different avatar does not create a new audience. If every account describes the same product with the same humor for the same people, you have mostly multiplied the credentials to manage. The network exists technically; its editorial logic is still missing.","Consider a note-taking app. One account can cover lectures, another fiction writing, another meeting notes. The demonstrations share a product, but their situations, references and success criteria change. That distance makes the experiments readable.","Write three sentences for each account: who it addresses, what it promises and what it refuses to publish. The last one does the most work. It stops every success elsewhere in the network from becoming an instruction to copy.","Isolation here is not a method for hiding account relationships or bypassing enforcement. It concerns distribution diversity. An audience that understands who is speaking is a more durable asset than infrastructure designed to remain incomprehensible."],"action":["Define an audience, a promise and a refusal for each account.","Compare comments for genuinely different uses.","Revise accounts whose roles overlap."],"trap":"Editorial differentiation should not be confused with technical concealment.","quote":"Another account is only useful when it brings another perspective.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Another account is only useful when it brings another perspective.","text":"Account Isolation: differentiate the voices before multiplying the profiles.","media":"/images/current.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Account Isolation","text":"Account Isolation is the AGD principle that gives every account a sufficiently distinct identity, audience and purpose to operate as an independent editorial surface.","media":"/images/current.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Editorial differentiation should not be confused with technical concealment.","media":"/images/current.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Define an audience, a promise and a refusal for each account.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/current.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Compare comments for genuinely different uses.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/current.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 3","title":"Revise accounts whose roles overlap.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/current.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"Write the refusal before the publishing plan.","paragraphs":["The most useful line in an account brief may be the one beginning “we do not”. An account teaching students to organise lecture notes does not publish generic founder motivation. An account helping managers prepare meetings does not suddenly become a campus meme page because a joke performed well elsewhere. These refusals protect an audience promise. Without them, every promising result in the network becomes a reason to make the accounts converge, until their supposed diversity consists of profile pictures and passwords.","Run a small editorial sorting exercise before scaling. Place recent posts from several accounts in one folder without names. Ask a teammate to group them by intended viewer and situation. Discuss the ambiguous posts, rather than treating the exercise as a scientific score. Then compare the language of genuine audience responses. Are viewers asking distinct questions, or are the same vague reactions appearing everywhere? Neither exercise proves that platforms reward isolation. They help you decide whether the network contains different editorial assets, which is the version of isolation worth building around.","Try writing the reason to follow each account on separate cards. One might promise practical editing breakdowns, another might explain the economics of creator tools, and a third might document a particular learning project. Now assign ten proposed posts. If every post fits every card equally well, the accounts are not yet differentiated. If one card cannot support a useful post without borrowing the other two accounts' material, its editorial role may be too thin. This exercise costs less than opening another production queue and makes the eventual account brief much easier to write.","The boundary should also help the operator make exclusions. A joke can be excellent and still belong elsewhere. An offer can be relevant to the business and irrelevant to the audience that followed this account. Keep those decisions in the brief so a new editor does not have to reconstruct them from a mood board. Review audience responses for evidence that the promise is understood, while remembering that commenters are a selective part of the audience. Account isolation is successful as an editorial practice when it produces distinct, understandable reasons to follow. It is not a claim that accounts can be made invisible to platform systems or immune to shared operational risks."],"diagram":{"kind":"compare","title":"An account brief with actual boundaries","items":[{"label":"For","detail":"A precise viewer and the recurring situation they face.","value":0},{"label":"Because","detail":"The useful promise a follower can describe to a friend.","value":0},{"label":"Never","detail":"The tempting content this account deliberately refuses.","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"Use the example to identify the narrator’s point of view, not merely their visual identity. Ask which other account could publish it without changing anything. If the answer is almost every account in your plan, your differentiation probably needs work.","caseIds":[]},"examples":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:45:45.218Z","author":"organic-club-editorial","media":{"kind":"illustration","src":"/images/current.jpg","width":1536,"height":1024,"alt":{"en":"Silver fish diverge into separate directions through a dark ocean."},"credit":"THE ORGANIC CLUB Studio","provenance":"Original AI-generated editorial illustration created for this publication on September 8, 2026. Not a documentary photograph.","source":"https://naybu256.github.io/images/current.jpg","license":"Original artwork","licenseUrl":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/about/#images"}}}],"$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16"]}]
